Reflected XSS into HTML Context with Most Tags and Attributes Blocked

✅ Lab Solved

What I Learned

This lab had a reflected XSS vulnerability in the search function, but a WAF was blocking most common XSS payloads.

Instead of using the usual payloads, I first checked which HTML tags and event handlers were still allowed. After finding an allowed combination, I created a payload that executed JavaScript automatically and called print().

The challenge was understanding that even when many tags and attributes are blocked, a single overlooked tag or event can still lead to XSS.

Key Takeaways
WAF protection does not always stop XSS.
Blacklist-based filtering can often be bypassed.
Testing allowed tags and events is important.
Reflected XSS can still exist in heavily filtered applications.
Always look for what is allowed, not only what is blocked.
